const TBE_JOURNALS = [{"name":"TBE Solo: Quick Reference","page":"How to play solo in Foundry","content":"<h2>The Broken Empires, solo in Foundry</h2>\n<p>Everything in this pack is a macro or a roll table. Nothing overrides your game system, so it works on top of Call of Cthulhu 7e, Custom System Builder, or anything else.</p>\n\n<h3>The loop</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Frame the scene.</b> Run <b>TBE: Subverted Scene</b>, state your expectation, take what the die gives you.</li>\n<li><b>Act.</b> Roll with <b>TBE: Skill Roll</b> or <b>TBE: Opposed Roll</b>.</li>\n<li><b>Ask when you don't know.</b> <b>Ask the Weave</b>, with odds. Phrase the question so a Yes creates a complication.</li>\n<li><b>Interpret.</b> Doubles on the oracle fire a Random Event automatically. Go with your first instinct.</li>\n<li><b>Keep the list current.</b> Add NPCs, goals, and threads to <b>TBE: Empires List</b> as they matter, cross them off when they don't.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3>Ask the Weave chart</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"3\">\n<tr><th>Odds</th><th>Extreme Yes</th><th>Yes</th><th>No</th><th>Extreme No</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Certain</td><td>01-25</td><td>26-90</td><td>91-98</td><td>99-00</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Likely</td><td>01-17</td><td>18-70</td><td>71-93</td><td>94-00</td></tr>\n<tr><td>50/50</td><td>01-10</td><td>11-50</td><td>51-90</td><td>91-00</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Unlikely</td><td>01-07</td><td>08-30</td><td>31-83</td><td>84-00</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Impossible</td><td>01-02</td><td>03-10</td><td>11-75</td><td>76-00</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p>Doubles (11, 22 ... 99, 00) generate a Random Event on top of the answer.</p>\n\n<h3>What the roll macros implement</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Roll d100 under modified skill. Success Levels = the tens die, minimum 1 on any success.</li>\n<li>Critical success: doubles under the skill, or the skill value exactly. Adds +3 SL.</li>\n<li>Critical failure: doubles over the skill.</li>\n<li>01-05 always succeeds; 99-00 always fails. Skill 0 or less still succeeds on 01-04 and crits on 05.</li>\n<li>Skill over 100 cannot critically fail and adds bonus SL equal to the tens digit of the excess, minimum 1.</li>\n<li>Opposed rolls apply the full resolution ladder: SLs, then criticals, then higher die, then higher modified skill. Degree of Success = winner's SL minus loser's SL.</li>\n<li>Fixed Numbers act as an automatic success at that many SL, and lose ties to a rolled skill.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Extended Rolls &amp; Social Encounters</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>TBE: Extended Roll</b> (Ch.2) &mdash; a task that takes more than one roll: crafting, research, tracking, anything with a target Success Level total and an interval. Start one, have each participant \"make an attempt\" during the interval, then \"resolve the interval\": the single highest successful roll counts in full, up to two more successful rolls that same interval each add +1 SL, and a critical failure anywhere in the interval halves the accumulated total (round up). Reaching the required SLs succeeds; running out an optional Limit of intervals fails.</li>\n<li><b>TBE: Social Encounter</b> (Ch.13) &mdash; the same engine applied to a scene. <i>Static</i>: a hidden Tolerance (how many attempts, success or fail, before the NPC ends the audience) and a running SL total compared to an outcome table once the scene ends. The same skill auto-fails on a third consecutive use. Exceeding Tolerance ends things immediately and knocks 1d10 off the total first. <i>Competitive</i>: two or more sides each track their own total; a successful roll adds to your own side or subtracts from a rival's. Two sides race to a Victory Condition and the winner's Degree of Success (winner minus loser) sets the outcome tier; three or more sides (a council vote, say) resolve by whoever has the most support when the GM calls it, no DoS table needed.</li>\n<li>Both tools remember their state in the world between macro runs, so a negotiation or a months-long crafting project can span more than one session. The running totals are shown openly in the dialog and the chat card, the same as everything else in this pack &mdash; if you're running a group and want the book's Tolerance-is-secret rule to actually hold, keep this dialog to yourself the way you would a GM screen.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Solo house rules worth taking</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Enhanced Defense, Solo</b> and <b>Solo Constitution</b> (d20 Wound Die) free for your PC.</li>\n<li><b>Lone Wanderer</b> free if you use the full Travel rules.</li>\n<li>+2 NPC Tolerance in static social encounters.</li>\n<li>Hire NPC allies early. Solo combat is lethal.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Tables in this pack</h3>\n<p>TBE: Random Events, Event Randomizers I and II, Subverted Expectations, Opposing Difficulty, Empires List. Edit any of them freely, the macros read whatever is in the table.</p>\n"},{"name":"TBE: Status & Peril Reference","page":"Statuses, wounds, and perils","content":"<h2>TBE Status &amp; Peril Reference</h2>\n<p>Every status this pack can put on a token, grouped the way the book presents them (Ch.10 Combat, Ch.11 Wounds, Healing &amp; Perils, Ch.14 Weave Magic). \"Auto\" means <b>TBE: Attack</b>, <b>TBE: Wounds &amp; Recovery</b>, or <b>TBE: Cast</b> applies and clears it for you as part of the roll. \"Manual\" means nothing computes it yet &mdash; mark or clear it yourself from <b>TBE: Status Effects</b> when it comes up at the table. Open <b>TBE: Status</b> any time to see everything currently active on your character in one card, and to repaint the token icons if anything ever looks stale.</p>\n\n<h3>Wounds &amp; Impairment (p.172&ndash;173)</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"4\">\n<tr><th>Status</th><th>How it triggers</th><th>How it clears</th><th>Source</th></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Impaired: Body / R Arm / L Arm / R Leg / L Leg / Head</b></td><td>Wound Die + Toughness &le; the location's total WP</td><td>Heal &rarr; Remove an impairment, or the wound closing to 0 WP</td><td>Auto</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Stunned</b></td><td>First-time Head impairment on an <i>odd</i> Wound Die: lose your next action, can still defend or move</td><td>Automatic after one round</td><td>Auto</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Arm Useless</b></td><td>First-time Arm impairment on an <i>even</i> Wound Die: drop what's held, and the arm can't hold a weapon/shield or make any roll that needs it</td><td>Heal &rarr; Remove an impairment there</td><td>Auto</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Leg Hobbled</b></td><td>First-time Leg impairment on an <i>even</i> Wound Die: still standing, but Run/Charge are impossible</td><td>Heal &rarr; Remove an impairment there</td><td>Auto</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Shock</b></td><td>A second impairment anywhere, a Head impairment on an even Wound Die, or a failed Body Endurance roll. Drops the character Prone and nearly helpless. A PC may spend 3 Resolve to refuse it once.</td><td>Heal &rarr; Bring them out of Shock</td><td>Auto</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Dying</b></td><td>Total lethal WP exceeds Lethality Level (&#8968;Death Threshold &divide; 3&#8969;) while in Shock. Roll Wound Die + Toughness each round; die if &le; rounds elapsed. Natural 10 stabilizes.</td><td>WP reduced to Lethality Level or below (still in Shock)</td><td>Reflected on TBE: Status; full round-by-round tracking is manual</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Infected</b></td><td>Infection check (Journey arrival, Daily Time critical-failure on Recovery, travel Infection Event, or an infectious attack)</td><td>Heal &rarr; Purge infection from a wound</td><td>Auto (checks run from Wounds &amp; Recovery / Journey Leg)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Septic</b></td><td>A Sepsis check (d20 + Toughness vs. total infected WP) fails. &minus;30 to all skills; dies in 48 hours unless treated (Heal at &minus;10, twice) or amputated (emergency Heal at &minus;20)</td><td>Successful purge (costs 1 Lethality Level permanently) or amputation</td><td>Auto</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Combat Maneuver Riders (Ch.10)</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"4\">\n<tr><th>Status</th><th>What it does</th><th>Clears</th></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Unbalanced</b></td><td>&minus;20 to the target's next roll</td><td>After their next roll (remove by hand once spent)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Locked</b></td><td>No Fighting Withdrawal for the target</td><td>End of the exchange</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Disarmed</b></td><td>Weapon or shield knocked away</td><td>When they recover the item</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Disadvantaged</b></td><td>Compel Surrender succeeded: they fight at a disadvantage</td><td>They yield, or the fight ends</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Magic (Ch.14 &mdash; Weave Reaction Table)</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"4\">\n<tr><th>Status</th><th>Trigger</th></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Restrained</b></td><td>Weave Reaction result 18 (\"Restrained for 1d4 rounds\"). TBE: Cast rolls the duration and applies it to the caster automatically.</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px\">Fatigue-from-Reaction results (e.g. \"1 Fatigue\", \"1d4 Fatigue\") add straight to the Fatigue count below, automatically, from TBE: Cast.</p>\n\n<h3>Fatigue &amp; Travel (p.188&ndash;190)</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"4\">\n<tr><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th><th>Clears</th></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Fatigued</b> (a count, not on/off)</td><td>Marks against the Resolve track, right to left, from travel and exertion. When the whole track is spent-or-Fatigued, further Fatigue instead becomes a Weary/Deprived/Sleepless wound.</td><td>Rest: Safe removes 3, Neutral 2, Precarious 1, Dangerous 0</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Weary</b></td><td>1-point lethal wound to Body from ordinary Fatigue overflow. Lethal (counts toward Death Threshold and Infection checks) but never itself becomes infected.</td><td>Only by resting &mdash; falls by the same amount of Fatigue rest removes</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Deprived</b></td><td>1-point lethal wound to Body from lack of rations</td><td>A successful Rations roll, or otherwise eating</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Sleepless</b></td><td>1-point lethal wound to Head from lack of sleep</td><td>8 hours of uninterrupted sleep</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px\">All three fatigue-wounds: never require a Wound Die roll to take or increase, never stack more than one instance, and can't be treated with Heal or Recovery rolls &mdash; only rest/rations/sleep as listed.</p>\n\n<h3>Other Perils (Ch.11, p.187&ndash;191)</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"4\">\n<tr><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Blinded</b></td><td>&minus;50 to all sight-based skills; ranged attacks impossible</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Deafened</b></td><td>&minus;50 to all hearing/speech-based skills, including casting Weave spells or divine miracles</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Frostbite</b></td><td>Cold-based wound from extreme exposure (1d3 to a random location per hour, no armour protection)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Burning</b></td><td>Ongoing Burn wound from fire</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Poisoned</b></td><td>Non-wounding poison or disease effect (paralysis, nausea, etc). A Challenging (&minus;10) Heal roll can halve its remaining duration, once.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Feared</b></td><td>Failed an opposed Willpower roll vs. a Fear Rating: Fight (all rolls at &minus;20, no maneuvers), Flee (move away, no other actions), or Fall (drop Prone, defend only)</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px\">None of these are rolled automatically yet &mdash; mark them from TBE: Status Effects when they come up, and clear them the same way once the scene resolves.</p>\n\n<h3>Position &amp; Consciousness</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"4\">\n<tr><th>Status</th><th>How it triggers</th><th>How it clears</th><th>Source</th></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Prone</b></td><td>First-time Leg impairment on an <i>odd</i> Wound Die, dropping in Shock, or a maneuver rider (Trip, Shield Bash)</td><td>Standing back up (a move action), or Heal &rarr; Bring them out of Shock</td><td>Auto</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Unconscious</b></td><td>First-time Head impairment on an <i>even</i> Wound Die, or dropping in Shock from a hit to the Head</td><td>Heal &rarr; Bring them out of Shock</td><td>Auto</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Dead</b></td><td>The Death Threshold reaches 0</td><td>GM's call &mdash; toggle it off the token</td><td>Auto (TBE: Attack, TBE: Quick Combat)</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p style=\"font-size:12px\">On the native the-broken-empires system, Prone and Unconscious are real TBE statuses (the token icon is the record, same as every other row on this page) and Dead reuses Foundry's own built-in \"dead\" status effect &mdash; none of the three live in a separate condition box anymore.</p>\n"}];

(async () => {
  if (!game.user.isGM) return ui.notifications.error("Run the TBE installer as GM.");
  const report = { macros: 0, tables: 0, journal: 0, errors: [] };
  const fail = (what, err) => {
    report.errors.push(what + ": " + (err?.message ?? err));
    console.error("TBE | " + what, err);
  };

  console.log("TBE | installing on Foundry " + game.version + " | system " + game.system.id + " " + game.system.version);

  /* 1. Folders. Optional, so a folder failure never blocks the install. */
  const getFolder = async (name, type) => {
    try {
      const found = game.folders.find((f) => f.name === name && f.type === type);
      return found ?? (await Folder.create({ name, type }));
    } catch (err) {
      fail("folder " + type, err);
      return null;
    }
  };
  const macroFolder = await getFolder("TBE Solo", "Macro");
  const tableFolder = await getFolder("TBE Solo", "RollTable");
  const journalFolder = await getFolder("TBE Solo", "JournalEntry");

  /* 2. Macros first. Existing ones are updated in place so hotbar slots keep working. */
  for (const m of TBE_MACROS) {
    try {
      const old = game.macros.getName(m.name);
      if (old) {
        await old.update({ command: m.command, type: "script", scope: "global" });
        report.macros++;
        continue;
      }
      const base = { name: m.name, type: "script", scope: "global", command: m.command };
      if (macroFolder) base.folder = macroFolder.id;
      try {
        await Macro.create(Object.assign({ img: m.img }, base));
      } catch (imgErr) {
        console.warn("TBE | macro image rejected, retrying without it", imgErr);
        await Macro.create(base);
      }
      report.macros++;
    } catch (err) {
      fail("macro " + m.name, err);
    }
  }

  /* 3. Tables. Created empty, then filled with whichever result shape this build accepts. */
  const short = (s) => (s.length > 48 ? s.slice(0, 48) + "..." : s);
  const shapes = [
    (r) => ({ range: r[0], weight: 1, type: "text", name: short(r[1]), description: r[1] }),
    (r) => ({ range: r[0], weight: 1, name: short(r[1]), description: r[1] }),
    (r) => ({ range: r[0], weight: 1, type: 0, text: r[1] }),
    (r) => ({ range: r[0], weight: 1, text: r[1] })
  ];

  for (const t of TBE_TABLES) {
    try {
      const old = game.tables.getName(t.name);
      /* Never clobber an Empires List you have filled in. */
      if (old && t.name === "TBE: Empires List") { report.tables++; continue; }
      if (old) await old.delete();
      const base = { name: t.name, formula: "1d100", replacement: true, displayRoll: true };
      if (tableFolder) base.folder = tableFolder.id;
      const table = await RollTable.create(base);
      let filled = false;
      for (const shape of shapes) {
        try {
          const made = await table.createEmbeddedDocuments("TableResult", t.rows.map(shape));
          if (made && made.length) { filled = true; break; }
        } catch (shapeErr) {
          console.warn("TBE | result shape rejected for " + t.name, shapeErr);
        }
      }
      if (!filled) fail("table results " + t.name, "no accepted result shape");
      else report.tables++;
    } catch (err) {
      fail("table " + t.name, err);
    }
  }

  /* 4. Journals. */
  for (const j of TBE_JOURNALS) {
    try {
      const oldJournal = game.journal.getName(j.name);
      if (oldJournal) await oldJournal.delete();
      const base = {
        name: j.name,
        pages: [{ name: j.page, type: "text", text: { content: j.content, format: 1 } }]
      };
      if (journalFolder) base.folder = journalFolder.id;
      await JournalEntry.create(base);
      report.journal++;
    } catch (err) {
      fail("journal " + j.name, err);
    }
  }

  const summary =
    "TBE Solo: " + report.macros + "/" + TBE_MACROS.length + " macros, " +
    report.tables + "/" + TBE_TABLES.length + " tables, " + report.journal + "/" + TBE_JOURNALS.length + " journals.";
  console.log("TBE | " + summary, report);
  if (report.errors.length) {
    ui.notifications.error(summary + " " + report.errors.length + " problem(s), see console (F12).");
    console.error("TBE | problems:", report.errors);
  } else {
    ui.notifications.info(summary + " Done.");
  }
})();
